{
  "description": [
    "What a checkout's .vantage/space holds, as both of its readers read it: the server's spaceid.Parse and vantage-md's parsePlanningSpaceFile, which vantage-check reads the file with before it ever writes one.",
    "`text` is the whole file; `id` is the space id it holds, or null when it holds none. A reader drops one trailing newline, and a carriage return before it, and takes what is left only when it is 16 characters of lowercase RFC 4648 base32 (a-z, 2-7).",
    "`ids` are path segments as GET /api/spaces/{id} receives them: `valid` says whether the endpoint looks for that id at all, which it decides before it touches the filesystem.",
    "`configs` are a repository's .git/config, whole: `bare` says whether both readers take it for a bare repository, as git reads core.bare (last value wins; a key with no value is true; true, yes, on and 1 are true, case aside). A main checkout's linked worktrees are its own only when it is not bare: the server then answers for their ids, and the checker's hint names it."
  ],
